  "body": "## Problem\n\nAfter PR #3818 (#3747), fig8 with \"Pass starts at\" Inside or Outside still has 18 named lifts. A second review of #3818 found that these lifts are mostly a gap in the planner, not a real need:\n- 9 lifts give the reason \"would cross a cut\";\n- 9 lifts give the reason \"would leave the area\";\n- no lift is for a fixture.\n\n`pass_link` tries only the straight chord. It does not try `edge_route`, which walks the edge of the area. The ring links of `ring_links::link` use `edge_route`, but the pass links do not.\n\n## Expected\n\n- `pass_link` also tries `edge_route`, with the same proof (`linkable`, `chord_clears` on the cutter-centre area) before it lifts.\n- A lift stays only when no straight chord and no edge route is clear. It keeps its named reason.\n- The pin `lifts::fig8_start_sides_lift_only_with_a_named_reason` also checks a maximum count of lifts. Lower the maximum to the count that remains after the fix.\n\n## Notes\n\n- P1 by the maintainer's rule: each outcome issue of the #3741 family is P1.\n- The maintainer's words on #3741: the tool \"should have just followed the contour keeping its plan not lifting the tool\".\n- Related: #3822, #3743, #3750.\n",
